worthwhile-offer-39_outputs:
{"output": "Based on the context provided, from June 2024 to June 2025, non-work-related messages grew faster than work-related ones, increasing from 53% to over 70% of all usage. Education is highlighted as a major use case for ChatGPT: 10.2% of all user messages and 36% of Practical Guidance messages relate to Tutoring or Teaching. Since Practical Guidance accounts for roughly 29% of overall usage and has remained steady, a significant portion of the growth in non-work usage is likely driven by educational and tutoring requests.

Additionally, many user interactions classified as Writing are mostly modifications of user inputs rather than new creations, and education-related messages include tutoring, teaching, and general how-to advice. This suggests that a considerable fraction of the increasing non-work messages can be attributed to educational uses such as tutoring, teaching, and learning assistance.

In summary, the growth in non-work messages from June 2024 to June 2025 is likely supported substantially by increased use of ChatGPT for education and tutoring purposes, reflected in the sizable share of messages requesting tutoring, teaching, and practical guidance related to learning."}

roasted-event-66_outputs:
{"output": "Yo, check this out — from June 2024 to June 2025, the total daily messages shot up like a rocket, going from 451 million to a wild 2,627 million. That’s more than a 5x explosion in message volume! But here’s the kicker: the non-work-related messages didn’t just grow; they **blew up faster** than work-related ones. Non-work messages jumped from 53% to a massive 73% slice of the pie, while work messages dropped to just 27%.

This means ChatGPT isn’t just some corporate tool grinding through spreadsheets. Nah, it’s morphing into the go-to personal companion for curiosity, creativity, and everyday hustle — people are vibing with it more for life’s non-work stuff than for the 9-to-5 grind. The data screams: ChatGPT is officially leveled up beyond the office, powering everything from chill chats to side hustles and brain-busting Q&A, turning into an all-around digital sidekick.

In short: total message growth is insane, but the real magic is how non-work engagement is flexing harder, signaling the AI’s rise as a daily lifestyle powerhouse, not just a workplace cog. That’s the future of AI use, moonwalking out of the boardroom into the hands of everyone else. Mad dope!"}
